    ---
    
    ## CHRONICLE OF THE AURORA STACK — OFFICIAL ARCHIVE
    ### Entry 7.114: The Casting at the Shattered-Spire Assault's End
    
    **Date of Entry:** Cycle 9, Frost Zenith, the Frozen Peace
    **Period Documented:** Final hours of the Shattered-Spire Assault the Orca Incursion
    **Compiled by:** Ingniu Pelm'Realm, Junior Archivist, Aurora Stack Records Office
    **Sources:** Survivor depositions (fragmentary), E'frostlings damage assessments, physical evidence at casting site, testimony of the orca commander Thung Thrakrek (obtained under Vestigium∴moria protocols)
    
    ---
    
    ### EVENTS RECORDED
    
    By the third day of the Shattered-Spire Assault — or the fifth; the Stack's time-crystals had shattered with the eastern ridge, and no surviving witness agrees — the assault had exceeded every parameter the defenders understood. Gnarkzund Zaith's seven pods had moved past raiding posture into sustained occupation. The Wake-Singers' hunt-songs, focused through the artifact designated the Dreaming Tooth, turned the Stack's own crystalline architecture into resonance weapons. Spires cracked along harmonic lines. Three terraces fell inward. The aurora itself stuttered, and with it, the light-based defenses that Aurora Stack had maintained for generations.
    
    E'frostlings warehouses on Terrace Momiou: destroyed. Crystal reserves in the southern vaults: shattered by sympathetic vibration. Personnel unaccounted for: forty-three at last verified count. The list was never completed.
    
    The Midnight Claws and operatives of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, present under Flipper Accord defense obligations, held the lower eastern corridors. By the final hours, Gnarkzund Zaith's shamans had breached the inner crystal barriers using Slide Prism techniques. The defenders' counter-tactics — designed for raids, not sieges — had been exhausted. Fire-core reserves were critically depleted.
    
    What followed is documented from three penguin depositions and one orca account. All four contradict each other on duration. Three sources state the casting lasted seconds. Thung Thrakrek insists it lasted far longer — that he felt his pod-bonds snapping one by one, each severance audible, a frequency that filled his skull like the sound of something structural breaking apart. His flippers shook throughout the deposition.
    
    The Midnight Claws and shadow Covens' Order practitioners constructed Grulkzul Omega Strike in the blood-dark of those final hours. It was not a known technique. It was invented — pressure-depth blood-working fused with Nightshelf fire-knowledge in a configuration neither tradition had sanctioned or, by available evidence, fully understood. The casters severed their own pod-bonds. They spoke names. They opened their veins and channeled the pressure of the deep through fire-core material as catalyst.
    
    The ice did not crack. It ruptured. A violent decompression tore through the eastern ridge — aurora-light and flesh and stone rendered into the same scattered debris. Gnarkzund Zaith operational commander of the assault, was confirmed destroyed at the point of impact. His body was never recovered.
    
    The casters were dispersed — scattered across the deep like a corpse in a riptide. Their names should appear in this record. The section reserved for them remains incomplete. The roster of Midnight Claws operatives assigned to the eastern corridor was stored in a crystal register on Terrace Momiou. That register was among the E'frostlings losses cataloged above.
    
    ---
    
    ### SIGNIFICANCE
    
    Grulkzul Omega Strike ended the Shattered-Spire Assault It also ended every practitioner who cast it, destabilized the fire-core reserves that both colonies depended upon, and scored a corruption scar into the ice-memory of the lower terraces that has never been successfully cleansed. Ice-readers who access the casting site report a frequency matching the Dreaming Tooth's hum — the frequency that won't stop. The casting's fusion of Nightshelf fire-knowledge with orca-derived blood-working was performed without the Aurora Stack council's knowledge or consent. This fact later provided foundational argument for The Way∴ens position that hoarded knowledge permitted desperate, unaccountable acts. Cross-reference: Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith, Article VII.
    
    ---
    
    ### NOTABLE FIGURES
    
    **Gnarkzund Zaith — Orca assault commander. Bearer of Khrrak's Collapse and Gut Inversion scarification. Bond-mate of Thung Thrakrek Killed at point of impact. Body unrecovered.
    
    **Thung Thrakrek — Orca commander, surviving. Provided testimony under Vestigium∴moria. Left flank bears Lucatransiius's spear-scar. Only orca source for what Grulkzul Omega Strike felt from the receiving end.
    
    **The Wake-Singers** — Provided theological and operational coordination for the assault. Wielded the Dreaming Tooth to amplify pressure-magic. Descended into deep routes following the Incursion.
    
    **E'frostlings** — Merchant faction. Funded and supplied the Stack's defense. Losses: forty-three personnel, southern crystal reserves, Terrace Momiou infrastructure.
    
    ---
    
    ### CHRONICLER'S NOTES
    
    I have reviewed the casting site. The ice hums. Not a sound — a pressure behind the ear. Twelve Midnight Claws defenders remain unaccounted for. Whether this number represents casters, casualties, or both, I cannot determine. No authority survived to adjudicate. I have left the name-fields open in the formal register. If records surface, they will be entered. I do not expect records to surface.
    
    — Ingniu Pelm'Realm
