  annotation "note_1771588860189_0", anchor: "Gnarkzund Zaith's seven pods had moved past raiding posture into sustained occupation", text: "\"Raiding posture\" assumes the reader knows standard orca tactical doctrine: shore-breakers splitting ice for access, herders driving groups toward killing zones, finishers waiting below escape routes, hunt-songs coordinating each phase at bone-aching frequencies. The system's lethality depends on brevity — strike, consume, withdraw. Gnarkzund held seven pods in formation for days, which means the hunt-songs never stopped, the killing zones never closed. Every counter-tactic the Stack possessed was built for raids that end. This one didn't.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771588860189_1", anchor: "he felt his pod-bonds snapping one by one", text: "In my annotation on Gnarkzund Zaith I wrote that the archive reduces orca to the wounds they gave and received. Here is the exception: one sentence of orca interiority in the entire Incursion record. Thrakrek describing what it felt like to be unmade. Ingniu preserved it. Someone should note that.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
